*STACK AND QUEUE

PART 1: STACK
1. Definition of Stack
A stack is a linear data structure that follows the principle:

LIFO (Last In, First Out)
The element inserted last is removed first.

2. Stack Terminology

Top: Points to the most recently inserted element
Overflow: Condition when stack is full and insertion is attempted
Underflow: Condition when stack is empty and deletion is attempted

3. Stack Operations

Push: Insert an element at the top
Pop: Remove the top element
Peek / Top: View the top element
isEmpty / isFull

Time Complexity for all operations: O(1)

4. Stack Implementation

Array implementation
Linked list implementation
Dynamic array implementation

